 [![MVP integration](https://github.com/itz1508/OneShot/actions/workflows/mvp.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/itz1508/OneShot/actions/workflows/mvp.yml)
 [![Research and Audit](https://github.com/itz1508/OneShot/actions/workflows/audit-capabilities.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/itz1508/OneShot/actions/workflows/audit-capabilities.yml)
 
-## Six-stage workflow and its gates
+## OneShot — Automated Process-Context Workflow
 
-The user defines the outcome; Research records **what success looks like**, Audit Discovery inspects the repository, and Planning specifies the change. The host must admit Build before dispatching work to **Modal Sandbox**. Moving arrows illustrate the designed lifecycle; the complete workflow is **not yet connected through the MVP**.
+The table summarizes the intended responsibilities. The [workflow contract](.agents/contracts/workflow.yaml) defines their registered inputs, outputs, and host gates; it does not by itself prove that every route runs end to end.
+
+### Workflow
+
+| Sequence | Responsibility | Context and output |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | **Establish scope** | Inspects `git status`, relevant code, and contracts; defines the authorized implementation scope before any modification. |
+| 2 | **Research** | Establishes evidence, not implementation design. Investigates information, dependencies, and technical references; returns evidence, source references, and unresolved questions. |
+| 3 | **Audit Discovery** | Read-only repository inspection. Traces paths and dependencies, identifies gaps, and records grounded findings and candidate CodeIntent. |
+| 4 | **Planning** | Owns architecture and design decisions and the BuildSpecification. Performs code review, gap analysis, Scanner review, and dependency mapping. No source writes. |
+| 5 | **Validation & Admission** | Host-owned. The host validates and freezes the plan under default-deny; Build is admitted only after preflight checks pass. The frozen plan is the authorized implementation scope. |
+| 6 | **Build** | Executes only admitted operations; preconditions are checked at effect time. Runs in the sandbox, applies the patch, runs admitted checks, and records actual effects and evidence. |
+| 7 | **Independent E2E Verification** | Runs real E2E checks against the acceptance criteria using actual execution evidence. No self-certification. |
+
+### Automated process context
+
+**Context management operates within the workflow, not as additional workflow stages.**
+
+For every agent handoff:
+
+1. The system identifies the receiving agent's required inputs using its registered input contract.
+2. Relevant context is automatically selected and summarized where appropriate.
+3. Required upstream outputs, guidance, and artifact references are supplied to the receiving agent.
+4. The agent performs its assigned responsibility and returns the output defined by its contract.
+5. The system persists the output and makes the relevant result available to downstream consumers.
+
+Original artifacts remain authoritative. Summaries are contextual representations, not replacements for evidence, requirements, or source records.
+
+### Runtime notes
+
+Meta Muse Spark 1.3 is the configured default provider; Claude Agent SDK and Codex SDK are optional adapters. The `echo` provider is a test double. Keep secrets in environment variables. The [historical audit records](audit/) retain evidence from earlier checks; current readiness requires a fresh source audit and runtime verification.
+
+**Implementation status:** The declared workflow contracts, agent guidance, and runtime must be audited separately to determine which automated context operations and handoffs are connected end to end.
 
